## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a full CAPA program around a nuanced data-leak due to a race in schema evolution, ensuring cross-tenant and cross-region considerations are baked in.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, tenant/stream IDs, redaction configs, logs, RCA link
- Region-aware lifecycle: detect, contain, remediate, verify, close
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with linked artifacts
- Cross-tenant/region metrics: recurrence, MTTR, false positives; canary rollout
- RCA template and validation workflow

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (TypeScript)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  streamId: string;
  evidenceUri: string;
  redactionConfigId: string;
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'remediated'|'verified'|'closed';
  region: string;
  createdAt: string;
  linkedLogs?: string[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate with existing incident management and alerting tooling?
- How would you design canary validation across regions to prevent regression?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests building a CAPA program for cross-tenant log exposure caused by race conditions in multi-region deployments.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, redaction configs, tenantId, logs
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link logs/traces
- Metrics: exposure rate, MTTR, false positives
- RCA template and canary rollout plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express API to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const {tenantId, issue, evidence} = req.body;
  if(!tenantId || !issue) return res.status(400).send('bad input');
  // Persist CAPA skeleton (pseudo)
  res.status(201).send({id: 'capa-1', tenantId, issue});
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify false positives and tune the policy?
- What synthetic tests ensure coverage across regions during canary rollout?

